&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in computer science, electrical engineering, embedded systems, a comparable qualification, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years of professional embedded software development experience with strong Embedded C and Embedded C++ skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with ARM-based SoCs or microcontrollers, board bring-up and hardware-near development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Embedded Linux, Yocto, BitBake, OpenEmbedded, Device Tree, BSP integration and cross-compilation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Linux Kernel configuration, device drivers and bootloaders such as U-Boot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical target-hardware debugging experience using GDB and JTAG, SWD or comparable technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A structured approach to root-cause analysis and experience with Git and agile development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An excellent standard of written and spoken English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
